WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.277
From NVIDIA Research at CVPR 2023,

00:00:02.357 --> 00:00:06.783
this work closes a safety-critical gap in object
pose estimation.

00:00:06.863 --> 00:00:11.912
Standard two-stage pipelines detect keypoints, then
solve for the 6D pose,

00:00:11.992 --> 00:00:15.725
but give no guarantee on how wrong the answer might be.

00:00:15.805 --> 00:00:17.597
The authors add two pieces.

00:00:17.677 --> 00:00:23.974
Conformal keypoint detection turns heatmap
detections into circular or elliptical prediction

00:00:24.054 --> 00:00:28.826
sets that provably cover the true keypoints with a
chosen probability,

00:00:28.906 --> 00:00:30.143
say ninety percent.

00:00:30.223 --> 00:00:37.353
Geometric uncertainty propagation pushes those sets
through the geometry to form a Pose Uncertainty Set,

00:00:37.433 --> 00:00:39.640
or PURSE, covering the true pose.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:46.711
From PURSE they compute an average pose and use
semidefinite relaxation to bound the worst-case error.

00:00:46.791 --> 00:00:50.870
On LineMOD Occlusion, coverage is valid and the
bounds hold.
